<div class="article-body">
  <p class="text-sm text-base-content/70">
    Technical cookie behavior reviewed against this application build on 29 August 2026. This note describes the software behavior; the service owner remains responsible for legal approval and deployment-specific additions.
  </p>

  <h2>Essential cookies</h2>
  <p>
    This application uses essential cookies to keep a signed-in session active, protect forms against forged requests, retain the selected language and remember interface preferences. These cookies support features requested by the user and are not an advertising profile.
  </p>
  <p>
    Session cookies normally expire when the browser session ends. A small number of preference cookies can remain longer so the interface does not ask for the same setting on every visit.
  </p>

  <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
  <p>
    The current application code does not load an optional analytics script. If an instance operator adds analytics or another third-party tracker, that operator must update this page and provide an appropriate choice before enabling it.
  </p>

  <h2>Manage cookies</h2>
  <p>
    You can inspect, delete or block cookies in your browser privacy settings. Blocking essential cookies can prevent sign-in, form submission and saved preferences from working correctly.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <% if service_contact_email.present? %>
    <p>For questions about this instance, contact <%= mail_to service_contact_email %> before continuing.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p>The service operator has not configured a public contact address for this environment.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
